  "development_scheme": "Leave-one-month-out over the four development months. For a held-out month every residual variant is fitted on its declared training rows from the other months; candidates are scored on ALL rows of the held-out month (every label, no clipping) against the incumbent's development prediction. The development months' v9 comes from the frozen folds (scratch/seasonal, scratch/forward: seasonal fold for January/July, forward fold for November; scratch/december: the January-November refit) or, where a candidate says cross_fit, from the cross-fitted v7 on clock-present rows (missing-clock rows and the LIRF fill population always keep the fold value). The blend tables on the development months are the incumbent's out-of-sample fold predictions (January/July/November) and the cached January-November refit leaves (December), identical for baseline and candidates.",
