  "prediction_postprocess": "adsb-v24-v1",
  "prior_evidence": {
    "audit_20260918": "docs/audit_20260918/README.md section 2: removing the residual stage costs +0.95% mean over the development months; it is single-seed, fitted on matches_v11 (1,111 stands)",
    "closed_levers": "committee growth, blend weights, residual seed bag and scale, calibration, v19 surface features, test-time adaptation, arrival context, geometry, OPDI, other ADS-B networks (docs/adsb_v20, docs/audit_20260918, docs/tta_screen, docs/opdi)",
    "learning_curve": "docs/adsb_v24/learning_curve.json (tools/residual_learning_curve.py; the December-held-out series completed before this declaration, the January/July/November series were still running and are recorded with the selection): on December held out, the residual trained on November alone lowers the non-LIRF blend RMSE by 3.03%, on July alone 1.90%, January alone 2.22%, July+November 3.00%, January+November 3.21%, January+July 2.61%, all three 3.26%; the three-month set subsampled to one month's rows gives 2.63-2.74%. Reading: adjacent months matter most, off-season months add little, and rows still help (3.5x rows within the same mix: -0.65% blend). The ranking's July half currently has one summer month (July 2025) behind the residual; June and August 2025 are its adjacent months and are only reachable through cross-fitting.",
    "v7_month_value": "docs/adsb_v24/v7_month_value.json (tools/v7_month_value.py): on December's clock-present departures the v7 forward-fold components (January-September) score 199.83, the seasonal-fold components 202.98, the January-November refit 196.58 (-1.63% / -3.15%): v7 responds to adjacent months like the learners did (docs/december/month_value.json), most at LIRF (306 -> 296) and LTFM (211 -> 207), where v9 carries full or large weight."
  },
  "purpose": "Two levers that the v21 stack leaves on the table, developed on the four labelled development months (January, July, November, December 2025) and shipped through a twelve-month refit: (1) the v12 residual stage trained on all twelve months of 2025 instead of the four months that had an out-of-sample v9, made possible by cross-fitting v7's twelve timeline components in four month-group folds; (2) v7 itself refit on twelve months (the same recipe and counts, December added, like v23 did for the learners). Two bounded scans ride along: the residual on the newer 1,332-stand match tables, and a low-weight blend of the LIRF learner table on unmatched LIRF rows.",
  "require_paired_day_intervals_below_zero": true,
  "residual_model": {
    "applies_to": "v12's residual model (nb feature set, matched rows outside LIRF, weight 1.0, single booster, unchanged parameters and inner rounds rule); the nb_season feature set adds season_cos = cos(2*pi*(day_of_year-1)/365.25) (1 at New Year, -1 at the start of July), a label-free calendar feature so a twelve-month model can keep the season-matched behaviour the four-month model has implicitly",
    "blend": "post-hoc convex combination with the extra table adsb_full (candidate_values in tools/run_adsb_v11.py); a NaN learner value leaves the row unblended",
